# IMAP and SMTP fixtures are wire captures, not text files.
#
# Their CRLF framing is the thing under test: `IMAPLexer` deliberately REJECTS
# a bare LF, because accepting half of CRLF would let a newline inside a literal
# forge a line boundary. Git's default text handling normalised these to LF on
# commit, which produced the worst possible failure shape — the working tree
# kept its CRLF so the suite passed locally, while the committed blob had none,
# so a fresh clone would fail tests that had never been touched.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions.
Tests/RavenFeatureTests/Fixtures/** -text
